# Paths that exist in upstream gocryptfs but are intentionally absent from this
# fork. check-deletions.bash fails if any of them comes back.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# When upstream ADDS a file underneath a path we deleted, git reports no
# conflict: our side removed the parent, their side created something new, and
# the three-way merge silently takes theirs. Only files we deleted AND upstream
# MODIFIED show up as conflicts. The v2.6.1 merge picked up
# tests/reverse/force_owner_test.go and .github/dependabot.yml exactly this way,
# and nothing noticed.
#
# Both of those examples are listed below now, so that class is guarded. This
# file only guards what it lists, though -- if you delete something during a
# merge and do not add it here, the next merge quietly brings it back.
#
# FORMAT
#
# One repo-relative path per line. A directory entry covers everything beneath
# it. Blank lines and '#' comments are ignored. Keep grouped by subsystem.
# Paths may contain spaces; do not quote them.

